<valueSet id="2.16.840.1.113883.3.1937.777.100.11.18" name="vs-synthea-observation-value-snomed" displayName="Synthea Observation Values (SNOMED)" effectiveDate="2026-09-11T00:00:00" statusCode="draft" experimental="true" canonicalUri="http://synderai.net/fhir/ValueSet/vs-synthea-observation-value-snomed" lastModifiedDate="2026-09-11T00:00:00">
            <desc language="en-US">
                <p>Categorical observation values the SYNDERAI Synthea pipeline emits as text. Every concept is a SNOMED CT concept, confirmed active in the International Edition, version 20260901, via a CodeSystem/$lookup. Synthea writes these values as fully specified names, in part as names SNOMED has since retired, so each concept carries the literal string the pipeline
                    emits as a synonym. The pipeline resolves the string to the code with that synonym rather than through a concept map: the strings are SNOMED terms already and need no code system of their own. Where several strings denote one concept, they sit as several synonyms on it. The stage qualifiers are not laboratory values; they are carried here because the pipeline resolves every
                    categorical observation value through this one binding.</p>
                <div class="__artdecor_box aswarning">
                    <p>This artefact includes content from SNOMED Clinical Terms® (SNOMED CT®) which is copyright of the International Health Terminology Standards Development Organisation (IHTSDO). Implementers of these artefacts must have the appropriate SNOMED CT Affiliate license - for more
                        information contact http://www.snomed.org/snomed-ct/getsnomed-ct or info@snomed.org.</p>
                    <p>For testing and demo purposes only. Not a published terminology.</p>
                </div>
            </desc>
